Posttrain Demo

Educational style fine-tunes of Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B and
Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507, developed with MLX LM.
The Qwen bases are provided by the Qwen team under Apache License 2.0.
The adapters modify its behavior through supervised LoRA training; the local
tokenizer template is modified to disable thinking during training and inference.

The broader Haiku training data includes a filtered and modified subset of
Haiku DPO by Daniel van Strien, licensed under CC BY 4.0.
See haiku/ATTRIBUTION.md for the source, license link, and modifications.
That dataset's attribution and license are separate from this code's license.

The original Claudish 0.6B experiment uses original synthetic parody examples.
Claudish 4B combines original examples with filtered answers from angrygiraffe's
Claude-attributed instruction dataset, whose card declares Apache-2.0.
See claudish/v2/ATTRIBUTION.md for exact sources, revisions, and modifications.
Claudish is a Qwen-based style experiment, unaffiliated with Anthropic, and
contains no Claude model weights. Public style references and evidence limits
are documented in claudish/CLAUDISMS_RESEARCH.md.
